---
import DocsLayout from '../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
---
<DocsLayout
  title="Install"
  description="One line, four questions, about five minutes."
  current="install"
>
  <p>
    Open a fresh Claude Code session in any folder. Paste:
  </p>

  <pre><code>Install Think OS for me from https://github.com/dhirajsapkal/think-os</code></pre>

  <p>
    The agent clones the repo, finds <code>adapters/claude-code/INSTALL.md</code>,
    and follows it. You'll be asked four short questions — vault location,
    Basic Memory, plugin bundle, vault name — each with a recommended default
    you can click without typing.
  </p>

  <h2>What it touches</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Creates your vault at the chosen path (default <code>~/ThinkOS/vault</code>).</li>
    <li>Installs Basic Memory via <code>uv</code> if it isn't already there.</li>
    <li>Registers the basic-memory MCP at user scope in Claude Code.</li>
    <li>Writes a Think OS block into <code>~/.claude/CLAUDE.md</code> (between explicit BEGIN/END markers — never overwrites surrounding content).</li>
    <li>Copies Think OS slash commands to <code>~/.claude/commands/</code>.</li>
    <li>Optionally installs a curated plugin bundle (pm / eng / design / ops).</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Full playbook</h2>
  <p>
    For the agent-facing playbook the install follows, see
    <a href="https://github.com/dhirajsapkal/think-os/blob/main/adapters/claude-code/INSTALL.md">
      adapters/claude-code/INSTALL.md
    </a>
    in the repo.
  </p>
</DocsLayout>
